With the notable exception of deliberate and premeditated bones-stuffing,
I see bones files as being largely balance-neutral.

Sometimes I'll find a shallow-level, trivially-claimed bones pile
with some great items that make my early game a breeze -- but I
generally don't die that often until around Quest-ish anyway.

Other times, perhaps more frequent, I'll find a bones pile where whatever
killed the original player(s) is still a significant threat in my current
game. (Inept demon-summoners deserve special mention here.)

Most of the time, though, the bones I find provide little in the way
of either urgent threat or vital loot.

> The standard answer to "too hard", "play in Explore mode until you're
> better", is very unsatisfying to me.  What if there were a "difficulty
> setting", like many FPS games have?

Nethack has difficulty settings galore. The game itself is "hopelessly
easy" mode. Harder modes involve conducts, and harder still, combinations
of conducts.

Figuring out which conducts or combinations are relatively harder or
easier than others is, itself, part of the challenge.

